    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm doing an audit on a fintech app we're launching. can you give me a quick checklist for WCAG 2.1 compliance? specifically looking for stuff regarding color contrast ratios and screen reader compatibility for mobile.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Start by ensuring all text and high-contrast UI elements meet a minimum contrast ratio of 4.5:1 against their backgrounds, and avoid relying solely on color for conveying information since screen readers cannot \"see\" shades directly. For mobile screen readers, explicitly label all interactive elements and ensure dynamic content, like payments or navigation menus, announces its state changes clearly to the user. Finally, test your UI with JAWS or VoiceOver on actual mobile devices to verify that keyboard navigation and focus indicators remain at least 3:1 contrast without causing visual overlap on smaller screens.",
